{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 6,
  "simulation_id": "sim-03",
  "member_id": "johansson-goran",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B030",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and experimental development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B007",
    "B006"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "I change my preferred configuration from B007 to B030. The discussion has clarified that optical lattice clocks are not simply an anticipation of future applications: magic-wavelength confinement created a robust physical architecture that has independently reached the 10^-18 regime and changed the experimentally accessible domain of time and gravitation. Katori's originating concept and Ye's decisive experimental development form an unusually compact and complementary credit line. The citation should recognize that completed invention and development, without claiming discoveries that the clocks may enable only later.",
    "case_against": "B030 remains principally an enabling precision-measurement achievement, and its boundary with the wider optical-frequency-metrology lineage requires documentary care. I also continue to regard circuit QED as a profound and mature opening of a controllable quantum-optical regime. But its proposed three-person credit line is less readily delimited from the broader superconducting-circuit and cavity-QED lineage than the Katori-Ye configuration.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that reproducible 10^-18-class clock performance is itself prize-worthy because it opens a qualitatively new experimental regime, even before a particular new-physics result is attached to it.",
        "response": "I find this distinction persuasive. In quantum-device physics, a platform becomes a completed achievement when its defining physics is controllable and independently reproducible; the clock architecture now meets that standard. This addresses my earlier concern that the most dramatic fundamental applications remain prospective."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig favors observable geometric and topological phase effects, while acknowledging that the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase have distinct histories that must be joined by a carefully limited common principle.",
        "response": "I continue to value B042 highly for its conceptual reach, including its influence on modern quantum physics. The stated historical-boundary problem remains material in a single prize configuration. B030 presently has the clearer unit of achievement: a specific physical clock architecture, mature realization, and defensible two-person attribution."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce notes that circuit QED is a strong alternative but that its attribution extends beyond the proposed trio, whereas optical lattice clocks offer a sharper experimental milestone.",
        "response": "I agree after reassessing my own first-round preference. B007 opened a genuine new regime and remains my leading alternative, but its essential theoretical and experimental lineage is broader than the proposed credit line. That comparison favors B030 on exact attribution without diminishing circuit QED's scientific importance."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether documentary review can sharply distinguish the Katori-Ye lattice-clock achievement from the wider development of optical-frequency metrology.",
      "Whether the citation should mention magic-wavelength trapping explicitly or remain at the broader level of optical lattice clocks."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "My research career and current leadership role are closely connected to superconducting quantum technology, so I disclose a strong professional proximity to the subject of alternative B007. The supplied evidence identifies no specific collaboration or personal connection with Katori or Ye, nor with the proposed B007 laureates."
  }
}
